  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Remove the puff pastry from box and outer wrapping, then set on the counter to thaw slightly, 20-40 minutes. (The pastry is ready when it unfolds easily but is still cool to the touch.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (10 x 15-inch) sheet frozen puff pastry"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the puff pastry is thawed, line a baking sheet pan with parchment paper.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash, dry, and slide thyme leaves off the stems; discard the stems. Set aside.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "¼ small pkg fresh thyme"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place egg and water in a small bowl, then whisk to combine the egg wash. Set aside.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 egg\n1 tbsp water"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "On a lightly floured surface, roll out the pastry just enough to cut an 11-inch square from it, discarding any excess pastry. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 tbsp all-purpose flour"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place the wheel of Brie in the middle of the pastry. Spread the top and sides of the cheese with preserves, then sprinkle with thyme leaves. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (227 g) wheel brie cheese\n¼ cup apricot preserves"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Brush the exposed pastry around the Brie with some of the egg wash. Fold the pastry corners up over the cheese, overlapping neatly, and pinch the seams shut. Arrange the pastry, seam-side down, on the baking sheet and place in the refrigerator for 15 minutes. (Chill remaining egg wash for later use.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, preheat oven to 400°F.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Remove chilled pastry from the refrigerator. Brush with reserved egg wash, then sprinkle with salt. Make two small slits in the top of the pastry to allow steam to vent while baking.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ tsp flaky sea salt"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place baking sheet in the preheated oven and bake until pastry is golden brown and puffed, 25-30 minutes. Remove from oven and let stand, 5 minutes. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Transfer Brie en croûte to a platter. Serve with crackers, additional preserves, and pecans. Enjoy!\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (120 g) pkg water crackers\n¼ cup apricot preserves\n¼ cup pecan halves"
    }
  ],
